  <prompt>Owner 2026-09-30 (D13, D-12): Model 1 is a per-customer dedicated stamp and customer stamps are keyless. Make every document that governs or describes provisioning say so; amend ADR-028 for D13.</prompt>

  <goal>
    No current document describes Model 1 as a shared environment or a shared tier (history may stay, marked as
    history). ADR-028 carries the D13 amendment: customer stamps disable key/local auth on every data-plane resource
    where Azure allows it, and the BFF uses the stamp identity; Key Vault keeps only secrets with no managed-identity
    alternative. E-2 (OpenAI) stays until T186's live proof (T230's keyless proof, H13), then is retired. The project's
    MUST rules and ADR Tensions list reflect the landed state (the time-boxed Document Intelligence key tension closes
    with this task). Root CLAUDE.md pointer rows and `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` are updated; the /provision-environment
    skill describes the dedicated stamp.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>G12 (plan §4) lists the documents; a 2026-10-08 grep found ~30 files with shared-Model-1 wording (design.md 43 lines, spec.md 9, deployment guide 8, CHANGELOG 8, ADR-052 7, inventory 5, INFRASTRUCTURE-PACKAGING-STRATEGY 5, ci-cd-architecture 4, topology 3, infrastructure/README 3, provision-environment skill 2, plus C# comments). Some are legitimate history or legacy-value parsing (TenancyModel parser tests) and stay.</background>
